      "proof": "Direct substitution in C(w)=sum_j 3^(m-j)2^(a_1+...+a_(j-1)) gives the two closed forms. Their common descending arrangement has Cmax=81+103*2^K. Subtraction gives the gains. Both words have exactly three pairs a_i<a_j. Their common denominator is D=2^(K+5)-243. For K>=6, 309+16*2^K<D, while 81+65*2^K>D. Thus any route replacing the position-weighted gain by ordinary inversion count loses information required even by the affine word inequality.",
